Canvas and security rules
Your meeting with the school should produce answers to these exact questions:
- Will UNC provide a Canvas Developer Key?
- What Canvas domain(s) should the extension support?
- Which exact OAuth redirect URLs will they approve?
- Which read-only scopes/endpoints can you use?
- Can you use a Canvas test/beta environment?
- Is the extension allowed to read assignment and submission information for the logged-in user?
- What student-data retention/deletion requirements apply?
- Is Chrome/Edge extension distribution acceptable, or must it go through the Chrome Web Store?
Canvas developer keys can restrict OAuth redirect URIs and API scopes, so get those decisions in writing before building the real login flow. Instructure Developer Documentation Portal
Never put these in the extension or commit them to GitHub:
CANVAS_CLIENT_SECRET
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
DATABASE_PASSWORD
OAuth access tokens
Only use placeholders in .env.example, such as:
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
CANVAS_CLIENT_ID=
CANVAS_CLIENT_SECRET=
CANVAS_BASE_URL=
The extension should call your backend; the backend should handle the OAuth code exchange and secure Canvas calls. Do not place a Canvas client secret in the extension, because extension code can be inspected by its users.